{"title":"Career roadmap · Sous Chef","role":"Sous Chef","summary":"A Sous Chef is the second-in-command in a professional kitchen, supporting the Executive Chef/Chef de Cuisine with kitchen operations, food production, quality control, menu execution, staff supervision, inventory, food safety and service coordination.","facts":{"Current degree":"BHM / B.Sc Hospitality & Hotel Administration / BTTM","Course":"Culinary Arts"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For a Culinary Arts pathway, this is a strong direct alignment, although Sous Chef is normally a progression role rather than a first job."},{"type":"h","text":"Typical route:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Culinary Arts","Kitchen Internship","Commis Chef","Demi Chef de Partie","Chef de Partie","Junior Sous Chef","Sous Chef","Senior Sous Chef","Executive Sous Chef","Executive Chef"]}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career objective"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Master culinary fundamentals, kitchen operations, food safety and professional discipline. Build experience across multiple kitchen sections."}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Progress through Chef de Partie/Junior Sous Chef roles and develop team-management and kitchen-costing skills."}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Become Sous Chef/Executive Sous Chef and specialise in a cuisine, hotel segment or food-production environment."}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Progress toward Executive Chef, Culinary Director, Corporate Chef or independent culinary entrepreneurship."}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 1"},{"text":"Culinary fundamentals"},{"text":"Knife skills, stocks, sauces, cooking methods"},{"text":"Practical kitchen assessments"},{"text":"Technica